<title>RUSSIA: Russia to auction 15 trln rbls in bills, bonds.</title>
<headline>Russia to auction 15 trln rbls in bills, bonds.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's Finance Ministry will auction 10.00 trillion roubles of 152-day GKO discount Treasury bills (series 22078) and five trillion roubles of an additional tranche of 448-day OFZ interest-bearing bonds (series 24010) on March 26, the Central Bank said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Full details of the T-bill auction:</p>
<p>    Series number		  22078</p>
<p>    Issue volume		   10.00 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations		  1.00 million</p>
<p>    Issue date		     March 26, 1997</p>
<p>    Tenor			    252 days</p>
<p>    Maturity date		  December 3, 1997</p>
<p>Full details of the bond issue:</p>
<p>    Series number		  24010 (additional tranche)</p>
<p>    Issue volume		   5.00 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations		  1.00 million</p>
<p>    Issue date		     March 26, 1997</p>
<p>    Tenor (remaining)	    448 days</p>
<p>    Maturity date		  June 17, 1998</p>
<p>    Original issue date	  December 18, 1996</p>
<p>    Next coupon rate	     37.68 pct (187,884 rbls)</p>
<p>    Next coupon date	     June 18, 1997</p>
<p>On March 26 the Finance Ministry will also repay about 6.34 trillion roubles in maturing 217-day T-bills (series 22046).</p>
<p>The series 24010 bond closed on Tuesday at 100.13 to yield 33.96 percent.</p>
<p>--Julie Tolkacheva, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
